{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "A friend of mine last week has a mailing list from 5+ years ago from an old niche website that he would like to market a new website too.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5722988d5131bc7fabe235925609f7e4f906310610aaa035ce78d4479f074c71.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.74], [4, 0.74, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.22], [6, 1.22, 1.46], [7, 1.46, 1.56], [8, 1.56, 1.86], [9, 1.86, 2.28], [10, 2.28, 2.58], [12, 3.22, 3.52], [13, 3.52, 3.92], [14, 3.92, 4.42], [15, 4.42, 4.54], [16, 4.54, 4.78], [17, 4.78, 5.0], [18, 5.0, 5.52], [19, 5.52, 5.82], [20, 5.82, 6.02], [21, 6.02, 6.14], [22, 6.14, 6.3], [23, 6.3, 6.5], [24, 6.5, 6.76], [25, 6.76, 6.94], [26, 6.94, 7.08], [27, 7.08, 7.5]]}, {"text": "He asked for my advice on the cheapest and most effective solution for blasting out to this 100k user list.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7b7c44020a7234b78c2533b60d69779cd83b5009d76b7c3686da13333dab49f6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.42], [6, 1.42, 1.52], [7, 1.52, 1.84], [8, 1.84, 2.1], [9, 2.1, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.72], [11, 2.72, 3.22], [12, 3.22, 3.46], [13, 3.46, 3.84], [14, 3.84, 4.06], [15, 4.06, 4.22], [16, 4.22, 4.4], [17, 4.4, 5.02], [18, 5.02, 5.32], [19, 5.32, 5.7]]}, {"text": "I approached this problem with a few things in mind.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/99b61fdea0e8198befcbb9216383f85b97ec74413a9fd2a469c5854b2d6cd777.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.62], [2, 0.62, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 1.28], [4, 1.28, 1.48], [5, 1.48, 1.58], [6, 1.58, 1.72], [7, 1.72, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.46]]}, {"text": "Mail providers don’t trust emails from new domains and new email servers.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9f350fcb0fe7d9bf7a940a320cd8e97462ca2beb102174ffa9a6982b94256348.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.9], [3, 0.9, 1.14], [4, 1.14, 1.52], [5, 1.52, 1.82], [6, 1.82, 1.98], [7, 1.98, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.64], [9, 2.64, 2.82], [10, 2.82, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.46]]}, {"text": "Mail servers, much like websites, have a reputation score.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0ebe8d541d2dc2d65f1d84bc73799211880cc3bda82e85ad3e665077a04af6cc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.62], [2, 0.82, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.5], [5, 1.76, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.04], [7, 2.04, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.96]]}, {"text": "If a mail server thinks you blasting too much unwanted email, then they assume you’re a spam king and mark all emails sent from your address as spam.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d194ff12cc871f59e327d97b11502a2629e717f46da358a60651345d8dea0e53.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.28], [3, 0.46, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.34], [6, 1.34, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.2], [9, 2.2, 2.58], [10, 2.58, 2.92], [11, 3.3, 3.36], [12, 3.36, 3.5], [13, 3.5, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.06], [15, 4.06, 4.16], [16, 4.16, 4.42], [17, 4.42, 4.72], [18, 4.72, 4.92], [19, 4.92, 5.08], [20, 5.08, 5.32], [21, 5.32, 5.64], [22, 5.64, 5.94], [23, 5.94, 6.14], [24, 6.14, 6.3], [25, 6.3, 6.6], [26, 6.6, 6.82], [27, 6.82, 7.18]]}, {"text": "So the key take away is don’t let mail servers think you are spamming their users.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/40a51f431c3261aca2dd00dd1e069eb557ad8c4bfb5bb1a7d805d7190015a548.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.46], [5, 0.9, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 1.72], [8, 1.72, 1.92], [9, 1.92, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.58], [11, 2.58, 2.76], [12, 2.76, 2.86], [13, 2.86, 3.24], [14, 3.24, 3.44], [15, 3.44, 3.72]]}, {"text": "The best way to protect yourself getting a bad reputation is making sure you are sending to a legit email and you only send it once.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/055784b3d2a8af67611d5f07e854f956a220df7affe43c7abe217f5384d67861.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.88], [4, 0.88, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.56], [6, 1.56, 1.82], [7, 1.82, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.14], [9, 2.14, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.34], [12, 3.34, 3.64], [13, 3.64, 3.84], [14, 3.84, 3.94], [15, 3.94, 4.24], [16, 4.24, 4.52], [17, 4.52, 4.62], [18, 4.62, 4.88], [19, 4.88, 5.3], [20, 5.3, 6.0], [21, 6.0, 6.1], [22, 6.1, 6.34], [23, 6.34, 6.58], [24, 6.58, 6.74], [25, 6.74, 7.04]]}, {"text": "Since Mailgun’s IP addresses are have a high reputation, we opted to use them instead of rolling our own POP server.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8bfcbf3e342fb8302b09f31d68bddfaee39a7c517a6205ecdf274b2ebb695c3f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.74], [2, 0.74, 0.98], [3, 0.98, 1.38], [4, 1.38, 1.72], [5, 1.72, 1.98], [6, 1.98, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.26], [8, 2.26, 2.88], [9, 3.36, 3.52], [10, 3.52, 3.8], [11, 3.8, 4.0], [12, 4.0, 4.26], [13, 4.26, 4.42], [14, 4.42, 4.78], [15, 4.78, 4.96], [16, 4.96, 5.2], [17, 5.2, 5.4], [18, 5.4, 5.64], [19, 5.64, 5.86], [20, 5.86, 6.22]]}, {"text": "Plus they offer 10k emails sending for free.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4e536bcf3772d188cc291df91ebb11f80d95d1b2d369b59cb82037c5959c81af.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 1.32], [4, 1.32, 1.82], [5, 1.82, 2.26], [6, 2.26, 2.48], [7, 2.48, 2.76]]}, {"text": "In my script I validate an email 3 different ways before I determine if it is a legit email account.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/503c614066ed00f8599f8bd4872f0bc0ab9a343e605bc55936dc81de52eee582.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.58], [3, 0.78, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 1.14], [6, 1.36, 1.6], [8, 2.0, 2.32], [9, 2.32, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 2.92], [11, 2.92, 3.06], [12, 3.06, 3.38], [13, 3.38, 3.6], [14, 3.6, 3.68], [15, 3.68, 3.78], [16, 3.78, 3.88], [17, 3.88, 4.12], [18, 4.12, 4.46], [19, 4.46, 4.78]]}, {"text": "The first check is to see if the domain is even a valid domain name.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e6668df622bc43a894ad9f0f7b759d72eb1db04435e1508391ba19355b67b8b3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.14], [4, 1.14, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.58], [6, 1.58, 1.82], [7, 1.82, 1.92], [8, 1.92, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.46], [10, 2.46, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 2.82], [12, 2.82, 3.08], [13, 3.08, 3.44], [14, 3.44, 3.78]]}, {"text": "I use the gem [whois](https://github.com/weppos/whois) to verify the domain of the email is legit.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6f1bdde5eefe1ebb16b033965bd5dfcc323731edb9907384f6a1df6bee4ab127.mp3"}, {"text": "domain_from_email is just a hacky way of pulling out the domain from the email account.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f2603656b7083a4f2b8fc29c4b822eb2ec2c1dc52b2062bec1f0beca77ada460.mp3"}, {"text": "This would break if your email had a .co.uk domain, or anything with 2 dots in the tld, but most of the emails don’t fall into that category.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/074f7cb375f846a7458a1abf3f291069426a1f833e60314dbd1294a0d577fbd6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.08], [5, 1.08, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 1.72], [9, 2.76, 3.26], [10, 3.26, 3.94], [11, 3.94, 4.32], [12, 4.32, 4.52], [14, 4.74, 4.92], [15, 4.92, 5.08], [16, 5.08, 5.2], [17, 5.2, 5.68], [18, 6.24, 6.44], [19, 6.44, 6.68], [20, 6.68, 6.8], [21, 6.8, 6.9], [22, 6.9, 7.18], [23, 7.18, 7.54], [24, 7.54, 7.68], [25, 7.68, 7.9], [26, 7.9, 8.08], [27, 8.08, 8.6]]}, {"text": "So, now we know the domain is real, lets check the MX records to see if the domain even supports receiving emails.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ad5062d885381ba0d756de11f1572593f02ad7914d077aa92adf22c846c428f0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38], [1, 0.68, 1.04], [2, 1.04, 1.16], [3, 1.16, 1.28], [4, 1.28, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.7], [6, 1.7, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.26], [8, 2.76, 2.98], [9, 2.98, 3.12], [10, 3.12, 3.32], [11, 3.32, 3.48], [12, 3.48, 3.9], [13, 3.9, 4.18], [14, 4.18, 4.36], [15, 4.36, 4.48], [16, 4.48, 4.58], [17, 4.58, 4.84], [18, 4.84, 5.14], [19, 5.14, 5.5], [20, 5.5, 5.94], [21, 5.94, 6.38]]}, {"text": "This is using the valid_email gem.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dc2056939a6f2f500d9e01cd46791d7fe5d23c6fdef0793da1fbbf1975853901.mp3"}, {"text": "We could actually ask the mail server if the email address is legit, but that can be an unreliable source of information depending on how the machines are configured.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8fb06e7c3b85ae22eb5accc270188d8fbc8975af0021f9cc7b1fc1a1f6272caa.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 1.92], [8, 1.92, 1.98], [9, 1.98, 2.2], [10, 2.2, 2.5], [11, 2.5, 2.76], [12, 2.76, 3.04], [13, 3.16, 3.26], [14, 3.26, 3.42], [15, 3.42, 3.58], [16, 3.58, 3.7], [17, 3.7, 3.88], [18, 3.88, 4.46], [19, 4.46, 4.72], [20, 4.72, 4.94], [21, 4.94, 5.48], [22, 5.48, 5.86], [23, 5.86, 6.18], [24, 6.18, 6.34], [25, 6.34, 6.46], [26, 6.46, 6.74], [27, 6.74, 6.98], [28, 6.98, 7.42]]}, {"text": "Since there could be duplicate email addresses in this list or in case I need to restart the process, I need to keep track of who I have emailed already.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/68193127d648a8c7e3b4f5439af266b3d693cc440e7d6b24bbb86dea66290ed4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.22], [8, 2.22, 2.42], [9, 2.42, 2.76], [10, 2.76, 2.98], [11, 2.98, 3.08], [12, 3.08, 3.28], [13, 3.28, 3.42], [14, 3.42, 3.56], [15, 3.56, 3.7], [16, 3.7, 3.96], [17, 3.96, 4.18], [18, 4.18, 4.6], [19, 5.0, 5.16], [20, 5.16, 5.3], [21, 5.3, 5.44], [22, 5.44, 5.58], [23, 5.58, 5.84], [24, 5.84, 6.04], [25, 6.04, 6.26], [26, 6.26, 6.48], [27, 6.48, 6.62], [28, 6.62, 6.88], [29, 6.88, 7.32]]}, {"text": "So I check to see if I think I have seen this email before.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a157a86a5e90b824b399c05a62299434de455c0dccc43c38b574f09922c4be59.mp3"}, {"text": "Wrapping it all together, we have a check each of our validation methods.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/94c44ed485002a2f96f02e5d8942187478698d14797307f2c0f56a8e13972d21.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.32, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 1.08], [4, 1.3, 1.48], [5, 1.48, 1.72], [6, 1.72, 1.94], [7, 1.94, 2.18], [8, 2.18, 2.54], [9, 2.54, 2.72], [10, 2.72, 2.82], [11, 2.82, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.68]]}, {"text": "If any one of them fails, we throw an exception which makes note of it in the rescue method.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fe245f414e94d855157bb4d8eaae09d9dfc439b0fb277e5b123807437455f6f8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 0.84], [4, 0.84, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.34], [6, 1.7, 1.76], [7, 1.76, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.18], [9, 2.18, 2.66], [10, 2.66, 2.98], [11, 2.98, 3.18], [12, 3.18, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.6], [14, 3.6, 3.72], [15, 3.72, 3.9], [16, 3.9, 4.0], [17, 4.0, 4.28], [18, 4.28, 4.6]]}, {"text": "I limit the run to 50 emails initially just so I can keep an eye on my mailgun reputation.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/72ef6ded2842bde944748bb56e8063e4f9aaef2dcbc1ce1c018c5145b5b8e00c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.88], [4, 0.88, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.84], [9, 2.84, 3.02], [10, 3.02, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.66], [14, 3.66, 3.92], [15, 3.92, 4.16], [16, 4.16, 4.34], [18, 4.8, 5.5]]}, {"text": "Because mailgun limits the number of emails that can be processed per hour, I am not going to bother threading this, since this will process much faster than mailgun will let me.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/021702387c1e824bc41d6c54226cf88d59ccad47b09e4f6757e0d6f013ee3ad1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [1, 0.4, 0.82], [2, 0.82, 1.14], [3, 1.14, 1.38], [4, 1.38, 1.62], [5, 1.62, 1.8], [6, 1.8, 2.02], [7, 2.02, 2.34], [8, 2.34, 2.5], [9, 2.5, 2.6], [10, 2.6, 2.98], [11, 2.98, 3.3], [12, 3.3, 3.62], [15, 4.24, 4.42], [16, 4.42, 4.68], [17, 4.68, 4.86], [18, 4.86, 5.12], [19, 5.12, 5.64], [20, 5.64, 5.98], [21, 6.22, 6.44], [22, 6.44, 6.68], [23, 6.68, 6.8], [24, 6.8, 7.2], [25, 7.2, 7.54], [26, 7.54, 8.08], [27, 8.08, 8.3], [28, 8.3, 8.7], [29, 8.7, 8.86], [30, 8.86, 9.04], [31, 9.04, 9.24]]}]}